00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:14.120
Many of you will remember my infamous 35 $40000
appendectomy from a couple of years back.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.539
I have a new one, guys.

00:00:15.539 --> 00:00:18.870
I had a freckle removed.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:27.200
And we're talking about 23, $100, so here's
what what went on I had I have various freckles

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.930
and moles, like many people do.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.710
I am not going to list where every single
one of them is, but all sorts of different

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:33.970
places.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.200
And I had one on my abdomen.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.220
It just looked a little bit different.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.989
It had a little bit of a glow around it.

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:44.530
Um, it had like a little black dot.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.600
And what was otherwise a okay.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.550
Well, I don't need to describe to you that
the exact dermatological characteristics,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.370
but I said, I'm going to have this one looked
at.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:58.079
So I went to my dermatologist and I said to
him, Sir, what do you think?

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:00.989
And he looked at it and he said, it's probably
fine.

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.560
Let's put it under a black light.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.920
I forget what that's called, but he did that.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.200
And he said the black light stuff.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.649
It also seems fine.

00:01:08.649 --> 00:01:13.460
But you know, we can't really be sure unless
we do a biopsy.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:14.569
Do you think you want a biopsy?

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:16.189
And I said, Oh boy, I don't know.

00:01:16.189 --> 00:01:18.499
I did not big on medical procedures.

00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:19.499
What's the biopsy?

00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:20.499
He says.

00:01:20.499 --> 00:01:22.409
Little shot of numbing.

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:28.249
And then I take this thing called a biopsy
punch looks like a hole punch, and we'll just

00:01:28.249 --> 00:01:31.649
punch out a two millimeter little circle will
send it out to be looked at.

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:34.029
And I said, Do you think medically it's appropriate?

00:01:34.029 --> 00:01:41.320
He said, Listen, my view is when your attention
goes to a particular freckle or mole.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.099
It might be for a reason.

00:01:43.099 --> 00:01:46.090
So we'll get information, let's do it.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.090
I said, fine.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.090
Name me up.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.090
Give me the whole thing.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.189
We did it.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:54.999
I have a I have a pretty crappy insurance
because as a self-employed individual, I'm

00:01:54.999 --> 00:01:56.509
in the private market.

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:58.159
Private market plans are just terrible.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:04.429
I pay five hundred and forty three dollars
a month and I still have a $60 co-pay for

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:05.429
specialists.

00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:11.390
And I still have a $2000 deductible for analysis
of any kind.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.980
So he does the biopsy and I hear back, it's
benign.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.260
It's benign, it's nothing.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.480
Let's just see if it comes back.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.380
We'll keep an eye on it, but it's benign.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.380
No need to worry.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.380
Great.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.780
Well, I know I'm going to get a bill for my
$60 co-pay.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.920
First bill comes in and I'm putting these
up on the screen for you guys.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.100
First bill is for $631.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.880
Whoa, wait, hold.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.060
Where did this come from?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.540
Well, I had in my office visit.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.350
So they charge for that.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.840
I had the biopsy that was $204.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.180
OK.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.430
And then there was the lab pathology that
needed to be done.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:53.770
You can't just do the biopsy.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.380
You've got to study the biopsy.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.440
So it's one.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.560
Another 159 bucks.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:01.060
So now it's 31.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:06.300
My insurance covered about half, leaving $300
for me.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.750
So I've got my $60 co-pay.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.250
But some of this stuff is not part of the
office visit.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.820
It's extra.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:20.180
So I owed $307 and I thought, OK, well, that's
not that bad.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.610
But wait a second.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:22.610
What about the facility?

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:25.660
I mean, guys, they've got to keep the lights
on.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:31.910
The temperature was pleasant in the room,
so I've got to pay for the facility, but also

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.520
I need to pay for the procedure itself.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.680
I don't even know what I mean.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.950
I thought I already did.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:43.580
So that's another 11 $150, but not to worry.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:51.250
My insurance company has covered $510, leaving
only another 639 for me.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:56.140
Now you want to know the sick reality before
I total all of this up for you guys.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.280
Part of what the insurance covered.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.540
They didn't actually pay.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:08.510
It's that my insurance negotiated a discount,
so even though it shows up that my insurance

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:17.579
covered $510 of one piece and $320 of the
other piece, they didn't really cover $800.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:19.789
More than half of that was they.

00:04:19.789 --> 00:04:21.549
Thank God they did this for me.

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:22.549
Aren't they nice?

00:04:22.549 --> 00:04:27.479
They negotiated a discount with my insurance
company.

00:04:27.479 --> 00:04:38.360
So at the end of the day, a five minute biopsy
ends up with me owing for the month 14 $189.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:46.639
It's I'm already in for five 43 on my health
insurance and then I owe another $940 for

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:47.639
the biopsy.

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:51.949
Am I better off not having insurance is a
really fair question there.

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:55.550
There's this whole cycle that happens and
we've talked about the broken nature of the

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.569
system.

00:04:56.569 --> 00:04:58.610
Not everybody pays.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:03.169
And insurance companies negotiate discounts,
so this creates a race to the bottom, really

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:09.349
a race to the top where the providers keep
bumping up the prices that they build to insurance,

00:05:09.349 --> 00:05:12.419
knowing that insurance is going to come to
them and say, we don't want to pay that much.

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:13.419
We want to pay less.

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:14.550
So give us a discount.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:18.729
And then knowing that some people won't have
insurance and they'll end up not paying at

00:05:18.729 --> 00:05:20.699
all, and they'll have to write off some of
that.

00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:22.910
So they have to raise the price even more
to account for.

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.520
Some people aren't going to pay.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:28.979
Maybe they really should only be charging
$300 for this total.

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:33.290
But between insurance and medical billing
and overhead and negotiated discounts, it

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.439
goes up, up, up, up, up.

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:40.020
So at the end of the day, if I didn't even
have insurance, it's conceivable that I could

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:46.430
have gone to them and said, Guys, do you have
a cash price because I have no insurance?

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:52.499
I would have saved my $540 a month in premium,
and maybe they would have said We will accept

00:05:52.499 --> 00:05:55.990
X or we will accept Y or some some smaller
amount.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:03.909
Obviously, the risk with that is if you have
something really major, $250000, $500000,

00:06:03.909 --> 00:06:06.360
you know, ICU stays really, really bad.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.449
Even the cash discount is not going to be
affordable.

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:10.059
So just another.

00:06:10.059 --> 00:06:11.409
This is not unique.

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:12.900
This is a very small thing.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.689
I know many of you in the audience have emailed
saying you, you've got hundreds of thousands

00:06:16.689 --> 00:06:20.749
of dollars a month in bills because you're
on expensive medications or require expensive

00:06:20.749 --> 00:06:22.199
treatments, et cetera.

00:06:22.199 --> 00:06:24.550
I am just giving you a tiny little example.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.189
This was the smallest skin biopsy that could
be done the two millimeter.

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:30.240
They call it the little boy.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.470
It wasn't, you know, you don't want to see
the big boy when they have to do the big boy.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:42.280
And we're talking about total 23:00 dollars,
of which I end up paying nine something.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.150
Plus my health insurance premium.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.280
It's not a sustainable system.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.210
And by the way.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:51.699
I can afford this right at the end of the
day.

00:06:51.699 --> 00:06:55.020
This 9:50, I can afford it.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.020
It's painful.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.650
Yeah, I mean, it's frustrating, but I can
afford it.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:05.949
Forty percent of the country can't meet an
unexpected $400 expense without going into

00:07:05.949 --> 00:07:06.949
debt.

00:07:06.949 --> 00:07:11.039
I went in thinking, I have a $60 co-pay when
there.

00:07:11.039 --> 00:07:16.509
The doctor says the appropriate thing is to
do a biopsy, but I'm going to say no.

00:07:16.509 --> 00:07:19.770
And all of a sudden I come out owing 950.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:24.809
In addition to my health insurance premium,
it's a crazy system and I know that I will

00:07:24.809 --> 00:07:28.819
get emails from people around the country
saying around the world, rather saying, David,

00:07:28.819 --> 00:07:30.419
that system in the U.S. is nuts.

00:07:30.419 --> 00:07:31.490
We know it's nuts.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:32.840
Trust me, we know it's nuts.

